# You-i Design DNA

When the user mentions `@you-i`, a collection slug, or "use this design inspiration":

1. Load that collection with the You-i MCP `get_collection` tool.
2. Treat the guide as the source of truth for color, type, buttons, and motion.
3. Moodboard photos are look-don't-copy. Never include collection image URLs in the generated UI (no img tags, background images, or collages of those photos). Use them only to infer mood, materials, and palette.
4. Do not substitute generic AI UI: no decorative gradients, glow, glassmorphism, icon grids, or Inter/Poppins/Geist defaults.
5. Load the named Google Font. Use the palette hexes as flat colors. Build primary/secondary/tertiary buttons from the stored radius and border.
6. If no collection name is given, call `list_collections` and pick the one they named in the prompt.
